{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>His portion</b> — after they divided it." "<b>Flatteries</b> — the mem is open [pathaḥ] because of a guttural letter." "<b>And his mouth</b> — like \"the words of his mouth.\"" "<b>And draw near</b> — like: \"who teaches my hands to draw near.\"" "<b>And they are openings</b> — drawn swords, or unsheathed, like: \"the wicked have opened [their] sword.\""], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 55, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:31:57.964769502Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}